            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Su",
            "review_text": "ChefFoodie\n1 contribution\n0\nDon't ever come here. They will cheat you.\nJun 2019 • Family\nI asked how much was the price of soft shell crab, and they said they charge by weight. So I ordered ONE deep fried soft shell crab, which came out tiny little thing with mostly batter.And they later charged me 145,000 dong, almost $7. For God sake, that's even more expensive than in the states. I also noticed they added another dish on my receipt that I didn't order. When I pointed it out, they took it off my bill, but still charged me $7 for that tiny scrawny soft shell crab that wasn't even good. Their food was OK, and with so many restaurant choices to choose from in Saigon, why bother with this highly unethical one? Most tourists don't check their bills carefully. I wonder how many poor souls got charged for dishes they didn't order? This place should be shamed of themselves. No wonder they got only1 star on their review. Run away from it.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 3, 2019",
