            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Su",
            "review_text": "Eva-Quirinius\nParadise305 contributions\n0\nGreat food served by moody waitress\nAug 2014 • Business\nIn a main road yet a bit distant due to a beer garden type setting. Loads of waitresses busy with shuffling around bottles of beer to keep them cold.\n\nWe ordered 3 main dishes, and for the fun of it the owner gave us an extra one:\n\nMorning glory with beef: tasty! And loads of veggies\nMini ribs: yes mini ribs, 1 inch max yet very succulent\nFried tahoe with herbs: the freebee, nice!\nFish: steamed on site in a spicy fish saucy dressing, yammie!\n\nPrices are good at 100-150k for a main course. Other guests mainly Vietnamese families so a good place to go local.\n\nAnd for the waitresses: well, some of them (there were many) were just grumpy. Maybe something to do with the high heels they were stumbling on...\nDon't let that ruin the evening though, enjoy!\nRead more\nWritten August 10, 2014",
